# Pairs with CursorNeverSkipsUnshipped. Reproduces the shipper half of #1060
# as a standing check: the merge also skips any entry whose HLC is at or below
# the scalar ship cursor - the highest HLC already acknowledged - and folds the
# partition cursor past it. One partition interleaves independent per-leaf
# clocks, so a genuinely new write routinely carries an HLC below the scalar
# cursor and is never shipped.
MODULE: CursorNeverSkipsUnshippedScalarHlcFilter
TARGET: CursorNeverSkipsUnshipped
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: skips entries at or below the scalar HLC cursor, so a new write with a lower HLC is never shipped (#1060)
PERTURBS: ShipSkip

--- FIND
       /\ ~ShouldShip(s, wal[s][i])
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the scalar HLC cursor is a skip criterion.
       /\ \/ ~ShouldShip(s, wal[s][i])
          \/ wal[s][i].h <= Max({wal[s][j].h : j \in {n \in 1..cursor[e] : ShouldShip(s, wal[s][n])}})
--- END
